14	
15	 <p>The value is split into declarations following the actual nesting of semicolons, parentheses, quoted
16	 strings, and CSS comments: a {@code ;} inside {@code url(...)}, another functional value, a string, or a
17	 comment never terminates a declaration. An unterminated quote, parenthesis, or comment does not throw and
18	 does not swallow later declarations — once it is clear the opener is never closed, the declaration
19	 containing it is treated as malformed and the following declarations are parsed afresh.</p>
20	
21	 <p>Each surviving declaration is kept verbatim, in its original position, unless it is dangerous or
22	 malformed:</p>
23	 <ul>
24	 <li>an {@code @import} rule, or any value containing a {@code url(...)}, is checked as a URL against the
25	 safelist's ordinary protocol rules (configurable protocols for {@code style} on the tag, falling back to
26	 {@code :all}, and defaulting to HTTP/HTTPS). Browsers interpret CSS escapes, control characters, and
27	 percent encoding when they read such a URL, so all of those normalizations are undone before the scheme is
28	 checked and cannot smuggle a {@code javascript:}, {@code vbscript:}, or unknown scheme;</li>
29	 <li>{@code data:} URLs are kept only when {@code data} is an explicitly allowed protocol and the media
30	 type is a safe (non-SVG) image type;</li>
31	 <li>the contents of comments and quoted strings are scanned by the same URL rules (a reference hidden
32	 there is still a rejected reference), but comment text is never mistaken for a declaration;</li>
33	 <li>everything else (ordinary colors, sizes, fonts, layout) is kept as written.</li>
34	 </ul>
35	
36	 <p>Only offending declarations are removed; neighboring safe declarations, other attributes, and text are
37	 untouched. If no declaration survives, {@link #clean} returns {@code null} so the caller removes the whole
38	 attribute.</p>
